{'sentiment score': 0, 'confidence': 0.0, 'reason': "FASB Accounting Standards Codification (ASC) Topic 810, Consolidation, ASC 820-10-15 - Line of Credit Facility Current Borrowing Capacity\n\nThe amount of current borrowing capacity under the credit facility considering any current restrictions on the amount that could be borrowed (for example, borrowings may be limited by the amount of current assets), but without considering any amounts currently outstanding under the facility.\n\nUS GAAP Accounting Standard ASC 820-10-15 defines this as 'the amount available to be drawn on the line of credit during the period'.\n\nThis is calculated by subtracting any restrictions on borrowing from the maximum borrowings allowed, and then adding back any amounts currently outstanding under the facility.\n\nFor example:\n\nMaximum borrowings: $100 million\n\nRestrictions: 50% of available assets (i.e. $25 million)\n\nCurrent borrowings outstanding: $20 million\n\nLine of credit current borrowing capacity = Maximum borrowings - Restrictions + Current borrowings outstanding\n\n= $100 million - $25 million + $20 million\n\n= $95 million\n\nTherefore, the line of credit facility has a current borrowing capacity of $95 million.\n\nThe key here is to calculate the maximum borrowings allowed and then subtract any restrictions on borrowing. Any amounts currently outstanding under the facility should be added back in as they are still available to be drawn upon during the period.\n\nIn this case, let's assume the company has a credit facility with the following details:\n\nMaximum borrowings: $100 million\n\nRestrictions: 50% of available assets (i.e. $25 million)\n\nCurrent borrowings outstanding: $20 million\n\ncalculation:\n\nLine of credit current borrowing capacity = Maximum borrowings - Restrictions + Current borrowings outstanding\n\n= $100 million - $25 million + $20 million\n\n= $95 million\n\nTherefore, the line of credit facility has a current borrowing capacity of $95 million.\n\nThis is calculated by subtracting any restrictions on borrowing from the maximum borrowings allowed, and then adding back any amounts currently outstanding under the facility. The result is the amount available to be drawn on the line of credit during the period.", 'company_name': 'COMPANY CONFORMED NAME:\t\t\tTENET HEALTHCARE CORP'}